                <pb facs="1209" n="1093" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg1093"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.93/112.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Consul Simpich</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-05-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 21, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Hostetter reports mobs looting Chinese stores Hermosillo. He has appealed to
                    Governor Maytorena for troops. Take up matter with Maytorena urging prompt
                    action for protection these foreign interests.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
